  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As the disc is revolving in circular motion about an axis passing through centre&nbsp;and perpendicular to its plane, thus centrifugal force must act on it. The forces acting on disc is shown below.</p><p>&nbsp;From FBD</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e19d503f-af31-481d-a3ec-b7bbd2925fe0-image.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 128px;\" /></p><p>For circular motion,&nbsp;frictional force must balance the required centripetal force.</p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>&#8805;</mo><mi>m</mi><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><msup><mi>&#969;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p>",
